 ## Overview
 
-Phial runs Fedora virtual machines on your desktop. Every secret stays on the host.
-A machine receives access to one secret for a set time and nothing more.
+Phial runs Fedora virtual machines on your desktop. Every secret and every private
+key stays on the host. A machine receives access to one secret or one key, for one
+machine, for a set time, and nothing more.
 
 The host is trusted. The machine is not trusted. Read [docs/DESIGN.md](docs/DESIGN.md)
-for the interface design and [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) for the engine design and the
-threat model.
+for the interface design, the gate design, and the threat model.
 
 ## Terms
 
 - A machine is one Fedora guest with its own disk, memory, and device list.
-- Env mode means that the machine reads a secret from a file.
+- A secret is a value in the keyring of the host, the Secret Service of the session.
+- Env mode means that the machine reads a secret from a file in its own share.
 - Proxy mode means that the host injects a secret into an outbound request.
-- A grant is a time box on one secret.
+- A key lives in the SSH agent of the session or in the GnuPG agent of the host.
+- A grant is a time box or a single use of one secret or key for one machine.
 - A share is a host directory that the machine mounts over virtiofs.
 
 ## Install
 
 Install the tools for the host setup:
 
-    sudo dnf install waypipe virt-firmware keepassxc pinentry-gnome3
+    sudo dnf install waypipe virt-firmware pinentry-gnome3
 
 Build the binary and install the pieces into your user directories:
 
