-## The Requests page
+- Port 5551 answers the SSH agent protocol. List returns only the keys that the
+  grants of the calling machine open. Sign asks the user with a host prompt
+  before it forwards to the agent of the session, once per key per minute.
+- Port 5552 carries the GnuPG agent protocol. A connection needs an open gpg
+  grant for the calling machine, and the user approves each connection with a
+  host prompt. The agent of the host still asks for the passphrase through its
+  own pinentry.
+- Port 4000 is the secret proxy. The path of a request names one secret, and the
+  gate answers only with an open grant for the calling machine. The gate injects
+  the Authorization header and rewrites the Host header to the upstream.
 
